  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Tesla Model Y mileage?",
      "a": "The Model Y reports the odometer signal over Tesla's cloud connection. To get a verifiable reading, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint (POST /v2/attestation/odometer-statement/:tokenId) with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the rawVC through the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect recharging on a Tesla Model Y?",
      "a": "Tesla's cloud connection lists the recharge event for the Model Y. Query the Telemetry API segments resource with the recharge detection mechanism, which uses charging signals and state of charge. The maximum date range per query is 31 days."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get a webhook when a Tesla Model Y starts charging?",
      "a": "Yes. Tesla's cloud connection provides the charging status signal. Create a Vehicle Triggers API webhook on vss.powertrainTractionBatteryChargingIsCharging with the condition valueNumber == 1, then subscribe the vehicle to it. Webhooks are in public beta."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I authenticate to read Tesla Model Y data?",
      "a": "Get a Developer JWT, then exchange it through the Token Exchange API for a Vehicle JWT for the specific vehicle. The vehicle must be shared with your Developer License first. Send the Vehicle JWT in the Authorization header of Telemetry API requests."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a Tesla Model Y vehicle data API for 2020 and newer model years, delivered through Tesla's OEM cloud connection. This coverage is tested, not just expected, and includes odometer, charge level, remaining range, tire pressure and charging signals for this EV. Once the owner shares the vehicle, you query the data with a Vehicle JWT through the Telemetry API's GraphQL endpoint."
